      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Error Boundary\nWhat it does\nCatches errors: getDerivedStateFromError stores the\nerror, and componentDidCatch logs it to the console.\nShows a fallback: the default screen says “Something\nwent wrong” and has three buttons: Try again (clears\nthe error and re-renders), Go to home and Call us (a tel:\nlink using PHONE_E164).\nShows the error message in development only\n(import.meta.env.DEV), so visitors never see technical\ndetails.\nResets on navigation: if you pass a resetKey and it\nchanges, the error clears automatically.\nAccepts a custom fallback through the\nFallbackComponent prop.\n\nIt’s mounted twice:\n\nmain.tsx, around everything, as a last-resort net. If the\ntheme provider or router itself crashes, the visitor still\ngets the fallback.\n\nApp.tsx, around the layout and pages, with\nresetKey={pathname}. A crash on one page clears when\nthe visitor navigates to another. It sits outside the\nheader and footer? No: it wraps MainLayout, so a crash\nin the header or footer also replaces the whole layout\nwith the fallback",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Error Boundary\nWhat it does\nCatches errors: getDerivedStateFromError stores the error, and componentDidCatch logs it to the console.\nShows a fallback: the default screen says “Something went wrong” and has three buttons: Try again (clears the error and re-renders), Go to home and Call us (a tel: link using PHONE_E164).\nShows the error message in development only (import.meta.env.DEV), so visitors never see technical details.\nResets on navigation: if you pass a resetKey and it changes, the error clears automatically.\nAccepts a custom fallback through the FallbackComponent prop.\n\nIt’s mounted twice:\n\nmain.tsx, around everything, as a last-resort net. If the theme provider or router itself crashes, the visitor still gets the fallback.\n\nApp.tsx, around the layout and pages, with resetKey={pathname}. A crash on one page clears when the visitor navigates to another. It sits outside the header and footer? No: it wraps MainLayout, so a crash in the header or footer also replaces the whole layout with the fallback",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
