      "text": "Header.tsx\n\nState: two flags, open (mobile menu) and scrolled (past 120px,\nupdated through requestAnimationFrame).\n\nOn scroll: the logo shrinks to 0.86, the wordmark gets smaller\nand the tagline collapses. The height stays fixed at 76px.\n\nDesktop: logo column, centred nav and an actions column. The\ntwo side columns are equal width, which keeps the nav centred.\nThe actions are Call Now (large screens only), the theme toggle\n(sm and up) and a hamburger below lg.\n\nMobile menu: a fixed full-screen navy panel under the header\nbar. When open, the bar itself turns navy so the close button is\nvisible. Links slide in with staggered delays. It locks scroll two\nways: body.overflow = hidden and Lenis stop(). It closes on any\nroute change.\n\nNav items: Home, About, Products (to /products/tmt-steel),\nBlog, Location and Contact. It’s defined in the file and not shared\nwith the footer.\n\n\nFooter.tsx\n\nSections: CTA band, then a 4-column grid (company, quick links,\nproducts, contact), the large outlined “Ramprasad” wordmark\nand the copyright bar.\n\nNew finding: the “CTA band” at the top has a headline (“Get TMT\nsteel, cement & materials at the right price”) but no buttons. It’s\na call to action with nothing to click. Add Call and WhatsApp\nbuttons.\n\nThe bottom bar has extra bottom padding on mobile so the\nfloating WhatsApp button doesn’t cover the copyright line.\n\nMissing from the footer: opening hours, a map link, and social or\nGoogle Business links.\n\n\nCoverIntro.tsx\nHow the effect works: the navy cover is position: sticky at top:\n76px with height 100svh - 76px. The rest of Home sits in a\nrounded-top panel (-mt-6, z-10, bg-paper) that slides up over\nit.\n\nScroll progress: a scroll listener sets a CSS variable --p from 0 to\n1, computed as scrollY / (window.innerHeight - 76). The cover\ncontent then moves up 40px and fades (opacity = 1 - 1.5p), and\nthe photo shifts 24px.\n\nMobile layout: brand, then photo, then highlights, in a 3-row\ngrid. Desktop uses two columns. The “Scroll to explore” button\ncalls scrollToY(innerHeight - offset).\n\nIt holds the page’s only <h1>. Reduced motion skips the scroll\nlistener, so the cover stays still while the content slides over.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Header.tsx\n\nState: two flags, open (mobile menu) and scrolled (past 120px, updated through requestAnimationFrame).\n\nOn scroll: the logo shrinks to 0.86, the wordmark gets smaller and the tagline collapses. The height stays fixed at 76px.\n\nDesktop: logo column, centred nav and an actions column. The two side columns are equal width, which keeps the nav centred. The actions are Call Now (large screens only), the theme toggle (sm and up) and a hamburger below lg.\n\nMobile menu: a fixed full-screen navy panel under the header bar. When open, the bar itself turns navy so the close button is visible. Links slide in with staggered delays. It locks scroll two ways: body.overflow = hidden and Lenis stop(). It closes on any route change.\n\nNav items: Home, About, Products (to /products/tmt-steel), Blog, Location and Contact. It’s defined in the file and not shared with the footer.\n\n\nFooter.tsx\n\nSections: CTA band, then a 4-column grid (company, quick links, products, contact), the large outlined “Ramprasad” wordmark and the copyright bar.\n\nNew finding: the “CTA band” at the top has a headline (“Get TMT steel, cement & materials at the right price”) but no buttons. It’s a call to action with nothing to click. Add Call and WhatsApp buttons.\n\nThe bottom bar has extra bottom padding on mobile so the floating WhatsApp button doesn’t cover the copyright line.\n\nMissing from the footer: opening hours, a map link, and social or Google Business links.\n\n\nCoverIntro.tsx\nHow the effect works: the navy cover is position: sticky at top: 76px with height 100svh - 76px. The rest of Home sits in a rounded-top panel (-mt-6, z-10, bg-paper) that slides up over it.\n\nScroll progress: a scroll listener sets a CSS variable --p from 0 to 1, computed as scrollY / (window.innerHeight - 76). The cover content then moves up 40px and fades (opacity = 1 - 1.5p), and the photo shifts 24px.\n\nMobile layout: brand, then photo, then highlights, in a 3-row grid. Desktop uses two columns. The “Scroll to explore” button calls scrollToY(innerHeight - offset).\n\nIt holds the page’s only <h1>. Reduced motion skips the scroll listener, so the cover stays still while the content slides over.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
