      "text": "contact.ts (the single source for business details)\n\nIt exports:\n\nBUSINESS_NAME, PHONE_NUMBER, PHONE_E164 (+917327855715), PHONE_DISPLAY (+91\n73278 55715) and WHATSAPP_NUMBER (91 plus the phone number)\nADDRESS (street, locality, region, postal code, one-line version), GEO (lat/long),\nMAPS_URL, DIRECTIONS_URL and MAPS_EMBED_URL\nENQUIRY_TEXT (the default WhatsApp message) and whatsappUrl(message)\n\nUsed by: ActionLink, Footer, Contact, Location, the Home JSON-LD, the form and the error\nboundary.\n\nIssues:\n\nA comment in the file says to confirm the number is actually on WhatsApp. Check that with the\nclient.\nSome places still bypass it: Home types 'Dhamara' directly, and “M/s Ramprasad\nEnterprises” and “Dosinga, Dhamara, Bhadrak” are typed in many components and in Meta.\nMissing constants that would remove other hard-coded values: SITE_URL (the Article\ncanonical is hard-coded to ramprasadenterprises.com), opening hours, email and\nsocial/Google Business links.\ncloudinary.ts\n\ncld(id, width = 1200) builds https://res.cloudinary.com/\n<cloud>/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto,w_<width>,c_limit/<id>. Local paths and full URLs\npass through unchanged. The cloud name comes from VITE_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME.\n\nIssues:\n\nIf that env var is missing, URLs silently become .../undefined/.... Add a guard or a dev\nwarning. Also set the variable in Vercel’s project settings, not only in your local .env.\nOnly the product pages use it. The cover photo and the hero slides are still imported locally\n(about 9.6 MB).\nIt has no srcset helper, so every browser gets one width. A small cldSrcSet(id, [400, 800,\n1200]) would let phones download far less.\nThe file uses CRLF line endings (the rest of the project is LF).\nsmoothScroll.ts\n\nA wrapper around Lenis. It keeps one instance and exposes helpers so other files don’t touch\nLenis directly:\n\ninitSmoothScroll() starts it with a requestAnimationFrame loop and returns a cleanup. It is\nskipped for reduced motion.\nscrollToTop, scrollToY, scrollToElement (default offset −96) and lockScroll (freeze scroll while\nthe mobile menu is open). If Lenis isn’t running, each falls back to native scrolling.\n\nIssues:\n\nThe rAF loop runs constantly, even when the page is idle.\nThe Footer’s back-to-top button bypasses these helpers (my main suspect for the jump).\nThe 96px offset is also typed in index.css as scroll-padding-top. Tie both to the header height.\ntheme.tsx\n\nThemeProvider and useTheme(). It starts from localStorage['theme'], or the OS setting if\nnothing is stored. It adds or removes the .dark class on <html>, sets color-scheme, and\nupdates the browser’s theme-color meta tag. It follows OS changes until the visitor picks a\ntheme manually. Storage access is wrapped in try/catch for Safari private mode.\n\nIssues:\n\nFlash of wrong theme. The class is applied in a useEffect after React loads, so someone with\ndark mode saved sees a brief light page. Fix with a tiny inline script in index.html that sets the\nclass before first paint. (I can’t see index.html, so check whether it already has one.)\ntoggleTheme writes to localStorage from inside a state updater. It works, but it’s an impure\nside effect that React’s Strict Mode may run twice. Harmless here, but cleaner to compute the\nnext value outside.\nutilis.ts\n\nOne function, cn(...), which is twMerge(clsx(...)). The name is a typo for utils. It is only\nimported by the dead components/ui/ files, so it goes away when you delete those (along\nwith clsx and tailwind-merge).",
      "fontSize": 11.902854759398489,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "contact.ts (the single source for business details)\n\nIt exports:\n\nBUSINESS_NAME, PHONE_NUMBER, PHONE_E164 (+917327855715), PHONE_DISPLAY (+91 73278 55715) and WHATSAPP_NUMBER (91 plus the phone number)\nADDRESS (street, locality, region, postal code, one-line version), GEO (lat/long), MAPS_URL, DIRECTIONS_URL and MAPS_EMBED_URL\nENQUIRY_TEXT (the default WhatsApp message) and whatsappUrl(message)\n\nUsed by: ActionLink, Footer, Contact, Location, the Home JSON-LD, the form and the error boundary.\n\nIssues:\n\nA comment in the file says to confirm the number is actually on WhatsApp. Check that with the client.\nSome places still bypass it: Home types 'Dhamara' directly, and “M/s Ramprasad Enterprises” and “Dosinga, Dhamara, Bhadrak” are typed in many components and in Meta.\nMissing constants that would remove other hard-coded values: SITE_URL (the Article canonical is hard-coded to ramprasadenterprises.com), opening hours, email and social/Google Business links.\ncloudinary.ts\n\ncld(id, width = 1200) builds https://res.cloudinary.com/<cloud>/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto,w_<width>,c_limit/<id>. Local paths and full URLs pass through unchanged. The cloud name comes from VITE_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME.\n\nIssues:\n\nIf that env var is missing, URLs silently become .../undefined/.... Add a guard or a dev warning. Also set the variable in Vercel’s project settings, not only in your local .env.\nOnly the product pages use it. The cover photo and the hero slides are still imported locally (about 9.6 MB).\nIt has no srcset helper, so every browser gets one width. A small cldSrcSet(id, [400, 800, 1200]) would let phones download far less.\nThe file uses CRLF line endings (the rest of the project is LF).\nsmoothScroll.ts\n\nA wrapper around Lenis. It keeps one instance and exposes helpers so other files don’t touch Lenis directly:\n\ninitSmoothScroll() starts it with a requestAnimationFrame loop and returns a cleanup. It is skipped for reduced motion.\nscrollToTop, scrollToY, scrollToElement (default offset −96) and lockScroll (freeze scroll while the mobile menu is open). If Lenis isn’t running, each falls back to native scrolling.\n\nIssues:\n\nThe rAF loop runs constantly, even when the page is idle.\nThe Footer’s back-to-top button bypasses these helpers (my main suspect for the jump).\nThe 96px offset is also typed in index.css as scroll-padding-top. Tie both to the header height.\ntheme.tsx\n\nThemeProvider and useTheme(). It starts from localStorage['theme'], or the OS setting if nothing is stored. It adds or removes the .dark class on <html>, sets color-scheme, and updates the browser’s theme-color meta tag. It follows OS changes until the visitor picks a theme manually. Storage access is wrapped in try/catch for Safari private mode.\n\nIssues:\n\nFlash of wrong theme. The class is applied in a useEffect after React loads, so someone with dark mode saved sees a brief light page. Fix with a tiny inline script in index.html that sets the class before first paint. (I can’t see index.html, so check whether it already has one.)\ntoggleTheme writes to localStorage from inside a state updater. It works, but it’s an impure side effect that React’s Strict Mode may run twice. Harmless here, but cleaner to compute the next value outside.\nutilis.ts\n\nOne function, cn(...), which is twMerge(clsx(...)). The name is a typo for utils. It is only imported by the dead components/ui/ files, so it goes away when you delete those (along with clsx and tailwind-merge).",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
